    "title": "Real-Time World Map (v1.03) powered By earth.nullschool.net",
    "description": "Real-Time World Map powered By https://earth.nullschool.net .\r\n\r\nFor more information please visit, https://earth.nullschool.net/about.html .\r\n\r\n22.06.26 Notes ===========================================\r\n\r\nHello everyone,\r\n\r\nThank you for liking and using the wallpaper I created. Due to my busy schedule in my personal life, I can only pursue software development as a hobby, and unfortunately, I don't have the time to update this project right now.\r\n\r\nRegarding the recent issues:\r\nAfter the latest Wallpaper Engine update, many web-based wallpapers have stopped working. The reason for this is the increased security measures in the new version (codes that display web pages using the iframe method are now blocked). In the future, either Wallpaper Engine will make an adjustment to fix this, or new projects adapted to the current rules will be released.\r\n\r\nIn the meantime, I wanted to share the temporary workaround I use myself: the version rollback method. I have explained the necessary steps below step-by-step with pictures.\r\n\r\n1.On the Wallpaper Engine page in your Steam Library, click the gear icon.\r\n2.Click on \"Properties...\".\r\n3.In the window that opens, select \"Game Versions & Betas\" from the left menu.\r\n4.Select \"previous\" from the list on the right.\r\n5.Close the window using the \"X\" button.\r\n6.Steam will now start an update process to install the older version of Wallpaper Engine.\r\n\r\nI hope this solution works for you!\r\n\r\n27.09.24 Update Notes =====================================\r\n\r\nMode-Overlay\r\n   -Air-Dew ===> Added\r\n   -Air-WBT ===> Added\r\n   -None ===> Added\r\n   -Bio-None ===> Deleted\r\n\r\nZoom\r\n   -Max limit ===> Old = 3000, New = 250000\r\n\r\nHD Mode ===> Added\r\n\r\nChange Unit ===> Added\r\n\r\nButtons Show/Hide ===> Added",
